    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 1 USER]\ne001\tOur small academic software group has built an open tool for exploring archival text collections.\ne002\tIt is not used for medical or individual decisions; it helps researchers find patterns and passages to inspect.\ne003\tTwo labs have used private builds and want us to release a public beta.\ne004\tThe analysis engine is stable on our test collections, but installation is awkward and the documentation assumes people understand our data format.\ne005\tHalf the team wants feedback now.\ne006\tThe maintainers worry a messy release will define our reputation.\n[Turn 1 ASSISTANT]\ne007\tThe decision depends on what you want the beta to learn and which failures would be informative rather than merely predictable.\ne008\tIf most early users will fail at installation or formatting, the feedback may tell you what you already know and consume goodwill.\ne009\tIf the private labs have only used familiar collections, a broader beta could reveal important assumptions.\ne010\tYou might delay “public” while expanding a structured preview to users with different data.",
